    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The scale of our solar system is difficult to imagine when we are standing on what appears to be a large planet looking at an apparently small Sun.  Pictures don’t help much. Although we could print the planet sizes to scale, the paper would need to be way too large to show the scaled distances.  Instead, to help understand the sizes and distances of our solar system, we’ve created a scale model.   This particular model uses a 2.5m vinyl balloon to represent the Sun.  Various marbles and balls generate models of the 8 planets, asteroids, and Kuiper belt objects. \r\n\r\nTwo versions of the activity are provided.  One is extensive and designed for school or informal science settings and perhaps permanent displays.  The other is a briefer version of the activity, designed for public science events.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
